================================================================================================================
[C3] rule 1 - the safety factor at four bits
================================================================================================================
  measured (pilot 18, 12-spectrum census at ell = 1e-3, p = 4):
    s = 1.01   -> 12/12 blow-up (state distance up to 6.1e34), floor at the cap
    s = 1.035  ->  0/12 blow-up, floor still at the cap
  cost of the damping at the benign ranges (same census):
    ell = 1e-1: 0.2166 -> 0.2208 (+1.9%),  ell = 1e-2: 0.877 -> 0.841 (-4.1%)
  on this run's four-seed d = 64 ladder the same move reads 1.412 -> 0.820 at ell = 1e-2 (where the undamped rule saturates) and 0.222 -> 0.218 at ell = 1e-1.
  so the damping is free; it removes the blow-up and not the floor, and both
  statements are what a rule has to carry.

